stationModels(scene)
    Return draw, animate and hit operations for the station's spatial presentation.
    Map graph x/y to horizontal x/z and graph z to vertical y.
    Render four module types, tubes and windows using instanced meshes.
    Show small physical blueprint models and names on the console.
    Highlight the selected blueprint and station module.
    Show six construction ports; hide ports with existing tubes.
    Show an adjacent blueprint only when the neighboring cell is empty.
    Keep generous three-dimensional pick volumes around the controls.
    Keep small additions anchored; fit larger graphs into the display bounds.
    Keep connection controls between adjacent occupied modules.
    hit(ray) returns the nearest visible module, blueprint or port order.
    animate draws at most twenty-four suited astronauts on the connected graph.
    Interpolate their travel, blend direction changes and animate arms and legs.
    Keep feet outside module shells and tube surfaces.
